     p:["Killingsworth and Gilbert built an iPhone app that pinged people at random moments and asked three questions: **what are you doing right now** (from 22 activities), **are you thinking about something other than what you are doing**, and **how are you feeling right now**.",
        "Two findings matter. Minds wander about **47%** of the time. And mind-wandering predicted **lower happiness** — people were less happy when their minds wandered, regardless of the activity. The wandering came first, so it is not simply that unpleasant activities cause wandering."],
